WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.781
Go where attention already is.

00:00:01.781 --> 00:00:02.850
Free places first.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.057
This lesson is about where buyers already hang out.

00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:08.551
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:12.114
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:12.114 --> 00:00:17.458
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:21.377
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:21.377 --> 00:00:25.296
Stay practical: name three hangouts before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:25.616 --> 00:00:29.703
Name communities, feeds, events, and inboxes your buyers already check.

00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:32.155
Remember the objective: name three hangouts.

00:00:32.155 --> 00:00:36.650
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:41.554
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:46.049
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:50.953
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:53.813
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:55.448
Feedback beats guessing alone.

